# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization.
#
# eol=lf is required, not cosmetic: without it, Git for Windows' default
# core.autocrlf=true materialises every text file as CRLF in the working tree.
# That breaks the byte-exact comparisons this repository relies on -- a CRLF
# copy of a registry seed makes `ros registry check` report every registry as
# stale against its own LF projection -- and a package built from such a
# checkout would ship CRLF files to consumers. This mirrors the .gitattributes
# this repository already scaffolds into the projects it installs
# (starter/*/gitattributes.template).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
